.IX Title "Lucy::Analysis::Inversion 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Analysis::Inversion 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Analysis::Inversion \- A collection of Tokens.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&    my $result = Lucy::Analysis::Inversion\->new;
\&
\&    while (my $token = $inversion\->next) {
\&        $result\->append($token);
\&    }
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
An Inversion is a collection of Token objects which you can add to, then
iterate over.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 3
\&    my $inversion = Lucy::Analysis::Inversion\->new(
\&        $seed,  # optional
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Create a new Inversion.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBseed\fR \- An initial Token to start things off, which may be
undef.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS append
.IX Subsection "append"
.Vb 1
\&    $inversion\->append($token);
.Ve
.PP
Tack a token onto the end of the Inversion.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBtoken\fR \- A Token.
.SS next
.IX Subsection "next"
.Vb 1
\&    my $token = $inversion\->next();
.Ve
.PP
Return the next token in the Inversion until out of tokens.
.SS reset
.IX Subsection "reset"
.Vb 1
\&    $inversion\->reset();
.Ve
.PP
Reset the Inversion’s iterator, so that the next call to \fBnext()\fR
returns the first Token in the inversion.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Analysis::Inversion isa Clownfish::Obj.
